{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Construction.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Construction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender mathutils vector construction blender mathutils vector construction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Construction.md","fileName":"Blender mathutils Vector Construction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender mathutils Vector Construction","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Embedded Python Internals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Embedded Python Internals","Blender mathutils VectorObject","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Construction.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Construction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender mathutils vector construction blender mathutils vector construction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Vector Construction.md","fileName":"Blender mathutils Vector Construction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender mathutils Vector Construction","heading":"Blender mathutils Vector Construction","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The `mathutils.Vector` constructor allocates or accepts a float array, initializes default components, and wraps that storage in a [[Blender mathutils VectorObject]]. The default no-argument path creates a three-component zero vector using CPython allocation and a blenlib fill utility.\n\nSpecialized creation functions distinguish copied, wrapped, callback-backed, and newly allocated storage. When the extension type supplies no allocator slot, a base-math macro creates the Python object through CPython's garbage-collected allocator be